# Trivy allowlist for the build-push CI pipeline (PETPLAT-105).
#
# The CI gate fails the build on any CRITICAL vulnerability in a service image
# BEFORE it is pushed to ECR. HIGH vulnerabilities are reported (artifact +
# job warning) but never block.
#
# To accept a specific CVE (e.g. no fix available, not exploitable in our
# usage), add its ID here — one per line — with a comment saying why and who
# accepted it. Trivy reads this file automatically (and the workflow also
# passes it explicitly via `trivyignores`).
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2023-12345   # <reason> — accepted by <name>, <date>, re-review <date>
#
# Review the current findings any time with:
#   docker buildx build --platform linux/arm64 --provenance=false \
#     --build-arg ARTIFACT_NAME=<jar-name> --build-arg EXPOSED_PORT=<port> \
#     -f docker/Dockerfile -t local/<service>:scan --load spring-petclinic-<service>/target
#   trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL local/<service>:scan
#
# --- accepted CVEs -----------------------------------------------------------
# (none yet)
